The {{Term/Store|Sensor|Sensors|Series, TotK}},{{Exp Game|TotK}}<ref name="Sensor">{{Cite|The Purah Pad Laboratory is ready for us to do some great things together! First, let's get that {{Color TotK|Red|sensor}} up and running.|Robbie|TotK}}</ref> also known as the {{Term/Store|Sheikah Sensor||BotW, AoC}},{{Exp Game|BotW, AoC}}<ref>{{Cite|{{Big|Sheikah Sensor}}|N/A|BotW}}</ref>{{Name Ref|AoC}} is a recurring [[Item]] in {{TLoZ Series}}.

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Stub|BotW}}
The Sheikah Sensor is used to locate [[Ancient Shrine]]s in {{BotW}}. It can be unlocked either by activating any [[Sheikah Tower]] after leaving the Great Plateau or in the [[Hateno Ancient Tech Lab]] by repairing the Sheikah Slate. When [[Link]] is near an Ancient Shrine, the Sheikah Sensor will beep louder. It can be upgraded to the [[Sheikah Sensor +]] in order to detect objects other than Ancient Shrines.

==={{TotK|-}}===
{{Stub|TotK}}
The Sensor is an upgrade for the [[Purah Pad]] used to locate [[Shrine of Light|Shrines of Light]] in {{TotK}}. It is obtained by speaking to [[Robbie]] at the [[Hateno Ancient Tech Lab]] during the "[[Hateno Village Research Lab]]" [[Side Adventure]].<ref name="Sensor"/> When [[Link]] is moving in the direction of a nearby Shrine of Light, it will beep louder, and it will display a message indicating if the Shrine of Light is directly above or below Link. It can be upgraded to the [[Sensor +]] to be used to detect objects that have been registered in the [[Hyrule Compendium]].

